WEBVTT

00:18.458 --> 00:19.333
Answer it.

00:21.125 --> 00:22.665
- Hello?
- Mr. Burroughs.

00:22.666 --> 00:24.499
My name is Detective Wayne Semsey.

00:24.500 --> 00:26.124
Is Warden Mackenzie okay?

00:26.125 --> 00:28.499
Tell them to back off,
pull the spike strip,

00:28.500 --> 00:29.999
or I'm gonna shoot him in the head.

00:30.000 --> 00:33.624
Confirmed. Suspect is armed
with a handgun on the hostage.

00:33.625 --> 00:36.249
Listen to me, David.
We can figure this out, all right--?

00:36.250 --> 00:38.333
Shut up! You're not listening! Drive!

00:42.375 --> 00:44.915
Suspect approaching
200 yards out, please advise.

00:44.916 --> 00:46.374
Listen to me, David, David--

00:46.375 --> 00:49.124
Pull the strip,
or I'll put a bullet in his head!

00:49.125 --> 00:50.707
Please, David, don't do this!

00:50.708 --> 00:53.083
- Pull the strip!
- A hundred yards.

00:53.666 --> 00:55.332
Pull the goddamn strip!

00:55.333 --> 00:57.332
Goddamn it, I'm gonna kill him!

00:57.333 --> 00:58.582
Pull the strip!

00:58.583 --> 01:00.375
- Fifty.
- Pull the strip!

01:15.375 --> 01:16.458
Now what?

01:17.083 --> 01:18.458
I'm open to suggestions.

01:21.375 --> 01:23.999
Burroughs's case
made national news five years ago

01:24.000 --> 01:27.749
when he was tried and convicted
for the murder of his three-year-old son,

01:27.750 --> 01:29.207
Matthew Burroughs.

01:29.208 --> 01:31.999
The nation had trouble reconciling
how a man could bludgeon

01:32.000 --> 01:36.040
his own son to death
with a baseball bat as he slept.

01:36.041 --> 01:38.375
So where is David Burroughs now?

01:39.291 --> 01:40.582
Hello?

01:40.583 --> 01:42.291
Rachel, it's David.

01:46.416 --> 01:48.957
David. What the hell is going on?

01:48.958 --> 01:51.333
I didn't mean to drag you into this,
but I need your help.

01:54.458 --> 01:55.458
Hey!

01:56.708 --> 01:57.958
Hello, Theodore.

01:58.875 --> 02:00.582
I hear Burroughs flew the coop.

02:00.583 --> 02:03.499
Listen to me, you piece of shit.
You tell them I'm out.

02:03.500 --> 02:04.500
Out?

02:05.125 --> 02:08.874
You were supposed to kill him,
and now he's a free man.

02:08.875 --> 02:12.249
- This wasn't my fault!
- Of course it was.

02:12.250 --> 02:13.832
But that's not your real problem.

02:13.833 --> 02:18.457
Your real problem is
you've been taking their money for years.

02:18.458 --> 02:20.790
I will pay them back. All of it.

02:20.791 --> 02:22.166
Even if you could,

02:23.416 --> 02:26.124
money leaves a trail.

02:26.125 --> 02:30.541
You, Teddy, you're a loose end.

02:31.333 --> 02:35.041
My advice? Take a page from Burroughs.

02:36.416 --> 02:39.375
Run, Teddy. Run.

02:43.000 --> 02:44.665
David, glad you called back.

02:44.666 --> 02:46.790
No, no, shut up, all right?
Tell the cops to back off.

02:46.791 --> 02:49.540
- And lose the chopper.
- I will. Just remain calm, David.

02:49.541 --> 02:52.500
They're turning
into the Greenville Outlet Mall.

02:54.291 --> 02:57.040
They entered the parking garage.
We've lost visual.

02:57.041 --> 03:00.499
David, we don't want to involve
innocent people here, right?

03:00.500 --> 03:01.915
We have visual again.

03:01.916 --> 03:03.457
They've left the garage
and are back on the road.

03:03.458 --> 03:05.332
I told you to pull the chopper!

03:05.333 --> 03:06.458
Let the warden go, David.

03:07.541 --> 03:09.541
Not until you pull the chopper!

03:10.125 --> 03:12.499
You let the warden go,
and I'll pull the chopper.

03:12.500 --> 03:15.708
They're slowing down.
Repeat, they're slowing down.

03:16.416 --> 03:19.290
The truck has stopped,
but the hostage is still inside.

03:19.291 --> 03:21.582
- Officers in position.
- Go! Go!

03:21.583 --> 03:24.041
Out of the truck! Out of the truck!

03:25.458 --> 03:26.708
Show me your hands!

03:29.250 --> 03:30.250
Go, go!

03:35.625 --> 03:37.833
- Suspect is not in the truck.
- David!

03:38.458 --> 03:40.125
What the hell is going on, David?

03:40.625 --> 03:42.166
Come on, David. Talk--

04:01.083 --> 04:02.875
Holy shit.

04:04.208 --> 04:05.624
It's fine. Just drive.

04:05.625 --> 04:07.541
- I am driving. This is driving.
- Okay.

04:08.125 --> 04:09.791
Just, when did you decide
to break out of prison?

04:11.375 --> 04:12.540
Kinda just happened.

04:12.541 --> 04:15.291
Kinda just happened?
That doesn't really… Okay.

04:16.916 --> 04:17.958
You have a plan, right?

04:18.875 --> 04:21.415
- David.
- I do, but you're not gonna like it.

04:21.416 --> 04:22.500
Oh, Jesus.

04:23.166 --> 04:25.958
I'm aiding and abetting a fugitive.
I mean, how much worse can it get?

04:26.750 --> 04:28.207
Rachel, you need to turn around.

04:28.208 --> 04:30.082
Back to where the cops are?

04:30.083 --> 04:32.041
Rachel, you got to trust me. Turn around.

05:07.583 --> 05:09.624
I was born

05:09.625 --> 05:12.290
In a crossfire hurricane…

05:12.291 --> 05:15.625
Special Agent Williams.
Nice job on the Galvin case.

05:16.250 --> 05:17.540
Thanks.

05:17.541 --> 05:18.958
I'm Simmons, by the way.

05:22.708 --> 05:23.625
I know.

05:24.208 --> 05:26.749
We actually studied
a few of your cases at Quantico.

05:26.750 --> 05:28.958
It's a real honor to be working for you.

05:29.458 --> 05:30.500
Anything else?

05:31.083 --> 05:32.208
Chopra's looking for you.

05:32.791 --> 05:34.082
Maybe lead with that next time.

05:34.083 --> 05:36.583
It's a gas, gas, gas

05:37.125 --> 05:38.250
Damn it.

05:42.041 --> 05:43.915
Got a second?

05:43.916 --> 05:45.207
Before you say anything,

05:45.208 --> 05:47.499
I followed protocol
commandeering that Mercedes

05:47.500 --> 05:49.999
no matter what that TikTok video
makes it look like.

05:50.000 --> 05:51.083
That's not why I'm here.

05:52.375 --> 05:55.208
Okay, um, then you can
forget what I just said.

05:57.541 --> 06:00.707
There's an opening
to lead the FTF out of Seattle.

06:00.708 --> 06:03.708
I know the agent in charge.
I'd like to recommend you for the job.

06:05.000 --> 06:05.915
Okay.

06:05.916 --> 06:08.082
I expected a little more enthusiasm.

06:08.083 --> 06:10.916
I-I am enthused, obviously. It's just…

06:11.958 --> 06:13.249
You caught me off guard.

06:13.250 --> 06:15.915
I always imagined
taking over here one day.

06:15.916 --> 06:18.665
You really think the great Max Williams
is ever gonna retire?

06:18.666 --> 06:20.708
No.

06:21.416 --> 06:24.208
Listen, you are a good agent.

06:24.916 --> 06:26.665
But that's not enough.

06:26.666 --> 06:28.749
You need someone in your corner.

06:28.750 --> 06:32.624
But if I'm gonna go out on a limb,
I need to know you're ready.

06:32.625 --> 06:34.457
That you want this.

06:34.458 --> 06:35.500
I'm ready.

06:36.583 --> 06:37.957
I want this.

06:37.958 --> 06:39.166
Good.

06:40.750 --> 06:41.832
Grab your stuff.

06:41.833 --> 06:44.750
- What's going on?
- David Burroughs just escaped from Briggs.

06:50.708 --> 06:52.415
All right, everybody on me!

06:52.416 --> 06:54.124
Details are still coming in,

06:54.125 --> 06:57.875
but we do know that Burroughs kidnapped
the warden before disappearing on his own.

06:58.458 --> 07:00.124
He's armed. Very dangerous.

07:00.125 --> 07:02.124
Been on the run for about an hour.

07:02.125 --> 07:03.457
What was this guy in for?

07:03.458 --> 07:05.665
- You're not from Boston, are you?
- No, why?

07:05.666 --> 07:09.000
Guy beat his own child to death
with a baseball bat five years ago.

07:10.333 --> 07:11.958
Prep packets are on board.

07:12.541 --> 07:14.249
Flight time is one hour.

07:14.250 --> 07:18.708
I want everyone up to speed
by the time we touch down.

07:21.500 --> 07:22.541
Not you.

07:25.000 --> 07:26.541
What were you and Julie talking about?

07:27.750 --> 07:29.541
That stupid TikTok video.

07:33.708 --> 07:34.958
Agent Williams.

07:36.791 --> 07:39.290
What? No. No.

07:39.291 --> 07:41.958
Keep them separated.
We'll be there in an hour.

07:43.791 --> 07:47.915
Apparently, the warden's son
was found tied up in his office.

07:47.916 --> 07:49.749
- What?
- Yeah, it gets better.

07:49.750 --> 07:51.415
That's where Burroughs got the uniform.

07:51.416 --> 07:53.249
The warden's son is a cop?

07:53.250 --> 07:54.374
From Revere.

07:54.375 --> 07:58.583
I want to know everything there is to know
about these Mackenzies before we land.

08:02.500 --> 08:04.582
I'm on scene at Briggs Penitentiary

08:04.583 --> 08:06.040
where just this morning,

08:06.041 --> 08:08.624
inmate David Burroughs
took the warden hostage

08:08.625 --> 08:11.165
and escaped through these very gates.

08:11.166 --> 08:15.290
Now, I can tell you that the warden
has since been released, however…

08:15.291 --> 08:16.583
I need to call Philip.

08:17.166 --> 08:21.166
Rachel, what the hell is going on?
You need to call me back. Please.

08:23.250 --> 08:27.415
Hey, sweetheart. I just heard.
They're saying he took the warden hostage.

08:27.416 --> 08:28.915
Are you okay?

08:28.916 --> 08:30.708
No. Rachel was there.

08:31.875 --> 08:33.416
- Where?
- Briggs.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.208
She called me yesterday,
said she was visiting him.

08:50.375 --> 08:52.082
This Wesson guy tried to kill you.

08:52.083 --> 08:53.833
You sure going to his house
is a good idea?

08:54.416 --> 08:56.000
He knows who has Matthew.

08:58.208 --> 08:59.832
You talk to your editor?

08:59.833 --> 09:02.082
Yeah, he's working on
getting us an address.

09:02.083 --> 09:03.582
You trust him?

09:03.583 --> 09:04.916
Jim? Yeah.

09:05.916 --> 09:07.665
Before you turned us
into Bonnie and Clyde,

09:07.666 --> 09:09.915
he was looking into Hilde Winslow for me.

09:09.916 --> 09:12.082
Turns out, after your trial,

09:12.083 --> 09:14.999
she changed her name, sold her house,

09:15.000 --> 09:16.665
and basically disappeared.

09:16.666 --> 09:18.915
- Disappeared?
- Yeah.

09:18.916 --> 09:22.458
He was able to dig up a PO box
in New York under her new name.

09:23.083 --> 09:23.916
Okay.

09:29.083 --> 09:30.458
Hey, let me…

09:33.708 --> 09:35.833
It's okay. All these years.

09:38.125 --> 09:39.791
I should've done something.

09:43.750 --> 09:44.916
I'm sorry.

09:46.958 --> 09:49.416
Hey, you're here now.

09:53.041 --> 09:55.166
You know Bonnie and Clyde died, right?

10:00.583 --> 10:02.500
Jim's got Wesson's address.

10:03.625 --> 10:05.708
He lives less than ten miles from here.

10:17.666 --> 10:18.541
Hello.

10:22.166 --> 10:23.791
And I can explain.

10:24.625 --> 10:28.041
You leave my family out of this!
They have nothing to do with it!

10:30.291 --> 10:31.791
I'll do whatever you say.

10:33.625 --> 10:34.625
Okay.

10:37.458 --> 10:39.000
You have my word.

10:44.416 --> 10:47.249
Hey, change of plans, uh, change of plans.

10:47.250 --> 10:50.540
You guys are gonna go up ahead,
and I will catch up later.

10:50.541 --> 10:52.375
You said that we were gonna go together.

10:53.250 --> 10:54.333
What's going on, Teddy?

10:54.916 --> 10:56.000
Nothing. It's…

10:57.541 --> 10:58.999
You gotta trust me on this.

10:59.000 --> 11:01.875
Um, you take Lisa,
you go to your sister's.

11:04.916 --> 11:06.875
- I love you.
- I love you.

11:07.541 --> 11:09.791
You be good for your mom, hmm?

11:10.375 --> 11:11.750
Why are you crying?

11:12.333 --> 11:13.500
Because I'm gonna…

11:14.083 --> 11:15.499
Because I'm gonna miss you.

11:15.500 --> 11:19.250
But you'll be there before bedtime, right?
We have to finish Harry Potter.

11:20.583 --> 11:22.708
I would like nothing more.

11:23.791 --> 11:25.416
I love you, Bug.

11:28.333 --> 11:30.541
Briggs Penitentiary,
where just this morning…

11:33.916 --> 11:37.124
We have everyone in the state
looking for him. We'll find him.

11:37.125 --> 11:39.249
They've done a really good job so far.

11:39.250 --> 11:42.082
Yeah, we're already here.
Might as well poke around a little.

11:42.083 --> 11:43.957
This is Deputy Warden Ralph Hitchens.

11:43.958 --> 11:46.499
He can answer
any of your operational questions.

11:46.500 --> 11:48.207
I'm gonna need
all visitor logs for Burroughs,

11:48.208 --> 11:51.290
plus a list of family, friends,
former inmates he might have crossed with.

11:51.291 --> 11:52.540
He's gonna need help on the outside.

11:52.541 --> 11:54.665
- I'm on it.
- So you say there's video?

11:54.666 --> 11:56.333
Yeah. Right here.

11:58.208 --> 12:01.208
They entered
the parking garage. We've lost visual.

12:02.541 --> 12:05.708
We have visual again. They've left
the garage and are back on the road.

12:06.708 --> 12:07.999
Where are the warden
and his son right now?

12:08.000 --> 12:10.040
Being checked out in the infirmary.

12:10.041 --> 12:13.957
Did the warden explain to you why he kept
driving if he was no longer a hostage?

12:13.958 --> 12:16.832
He said if he didn't, Burroughs would
start killing people at the mall.

12:16.833 --> 12:19.499
We searched the garage,
but we're not sure how he got out.

12:19.500 --> 12:24.207
Any reports of stolen cars from
the garage or carjackings in the area?

12:24.208 --> 12:25.207
No.

12:25.208 --> 12:26.166
Do the math.

12:27.291 --> 12:28.541
Someone picked him up.

12:29.166 --> 12:31.500
So you guys think he had an accomplice?

12:32.166 --> 12:34.250
Oh, he had more than one.

12:35.458 --> 12:37.125
Bring in the warden and his son.

12:38.083 --> 12:39.250
Right.

12:42.583 --> 12:44.290
Any of this adding up for you?

12:44.291 --> 12:47.249
Not even a little.
Burroughs is a model prisoner.

12:47.250 --> 12:49.624
He hasn't had a single
incident report in five years,

12:49.625 --> 12:52.582
and then all of a sudden,
in the last three days,

12:52.583 --> 12:55.791
he nearly beats an inmate to death,
tries to kill a guard, and escapes?

12:58.791 --> 13:00.625
So what happened three days ago?

13:05.500 --> 13:06.999
- Warden Mackenzie.
- Yeah.

13:07.000 --> 13:08.415
Agent Williams, Agent Greer.

13:08.416 --> 13:09.874
Oh, yeah? Nice to meet you.

13:09.875 --> 13:12.624
- This is my son, Adam.
- Sounds like you had a hell of a morning.

13:12.625 --> 13:14.290
You can say that again.

13:14.291 --> 13:16.124
Well, we just gotta go over a few things.

13:16.125 --> 13:17.415
Of course. Happy to help.

13:17.416 --> 13:21.582
Hmm. Detective Semsey was kind enough
to give us your version of the events.

13:21.583 --> 13:22.499
Our version?

13:22.500 --> 13:24.875
How exactly
did David Burroughs get your gun?

13:25.458 --> 13:27.582
Uh, the inmate caught me off guard.

13:27.583 --> 13:29.750
Inmate? That's how you refer to him?

13:31.291 --> 13:32.874
- Excuse me?
- Never mind that.

13:32.875 --> 13:38.040
We'll come back to it.
So, after the inmate caught you off guard,

13:38.041 --> 13:41.750
you just stripped down
and handed your uniform over.

13:43.625 --> 13:46.499
Uh, he had my gun.
What was I supposed to do?

13:46.500 --> 13:49.166
And was Burroughs handcuffed
during all of this, Officer Mackenzie?

13:49.750 --> 13:50.625
Yes.

13:51.333 --> 13:53.916
- And it's Sergeant Mackenzie.
- Oh, Sergeant.

13:55.125 --> 13:57.125
- You hear that, Sarah?
- I sure did.

13:57.708 --> 14:00.332
I guess they'll promote anybody
over at BPD.

14:00.333 --> 14:01.457
I guess so.

14:01.458 --> 14:05.332
Even a guy who's so inept,
he allowed a handcuffed inmate

14:05.333 --> 14:06.790
to reach into his jacket,

14:06.791 --> 14:09.457
unsnap his holster,
and pull out his pistol.

14:09.458 --> 14:13.124
You sure that's the statement
you want to stick with, Sergeant?

14:13.125 --> 14:14.832
Are you questioning my integrity?

14:14.833 --> 14:16.249
- What?
- You heard what I said.

14:16.250 --> 14:18.666
Take it easy, tiger.
How about you, Warden?

14:19.708 --> 14:22.624
Who do you think picked up Burroughs
after you dropped him off at the mall?

14:22.625 --> 14:24.249
Dropped him off?

14:24.250 --> 14:25.749
The inmate had a gun to my head.

14:25.750 --> 14:27.874
Told me to let him out, so I did.
End of story.

14:27.875 --> 14:29.625
Yeah, there goes that word again.

14:30.458 --> 14:31.540
"Inmate."

14:31.541 --> 14:34.499
You and David's father, Lenny,
worked Robbery-Homicide for 20 years.

14:34.500 --> 14:36.624
Adam and David grew up together.
You were family.

14:36.625 --> 14:38.665
Doesn't mean we helped.
In fact, that's probably--

14:38.666 --> 14:39.832
You know what? You're right.

14:39.833 --> 14:43.499
That's probably how Burroughs got the jump
on childhood best friend here,

14:43.500 --> 14:45.832
while you agreed to chauffeur.

14:45.833 --> 14:48.916
Quit talking to me like
I'm a goddamn idiot. Who picked him up?

14:50.458 --> 14:52.375
I think we're done talking
without a lawyer.

14:53.750 --> 14:54.916
Agent Greer.

14:56.083 --> 14:57.415
Thank you.

14:57.416 --> 14:59.082
What do you got there, Agent Greer?

14:59.083 --> 15:01.166
- Visitor logs for David Burroughs.
- Oh.

15:02.125 --> 15:04.082
Anything interesting in there?

15:04.083 --> 15:05.208
I'd say so.

15:05.791 --> 15:08.374
Burroughs hasn't had a single visitor
for five years,

15:08.375 --> 15:11.833
but guess who showed up
three days ago before he escaped?

15:12.416 --> 15:13.332
Who?

15:13.333 --> 15:16.625
Rachel Mills. His ex-sister-in-law.

15:17.416 --> 15:19.208
You don't say.

15:21.291 --> 15:23.832
Think we can get a BOLO out
on Rachel Mills?

15:23.833 --> 15:25.125
Mm-hmm.

15:28.416 --> 15:30.541
Looks like you and Sonny Boy
are gonna need that lawyer.

15:40.083 --> 15:42.333
We'll be at Wesson's in a few minutes.

15:46.125 --> 15:48.541
She's probably seen this
on the news by now.

15:49.333 --> 15:50.915
You know what?
I'm gonna power down anyway.

15:50.916 --> 15:52.499
The police can ping cell towers.

15:52.500 --> 15:54.291
Did you tell her about Matthew?

15:54.916 --> 15:56.290
I tried.

15:56.291 --> 15:57.416
Didn't go well.

15:58.750 --> 16:00.665
- Rachel…
- I know.

16:00.666 --> 16:02.125
It's not that simple.

16:03.666 --> 16:05.291
After Matthew…

16:10.083 --> 16:14.082
I wasn't sure she'd be able
to put the pieces back together again.

16:14.083 --> 16:15.416
She finally has.

16:17.916 --> 16:19.540
So she's happy?

16:19.541 --> 16:20.666
Yeah.

16:21.500 --> 16:22.583
She's remarried.

16:25.083 --> 16:27.750
They're expecting a baby girl soon.

16:30.000 --> 16:31.957
I'm in charge of the baby shower.

16:31.958 --> 16:34.124
I mean, I'm not in charge, in charge,

16:34.125 --> 16:36.707
I'm more like a puppet dictator
quashing the dissidents

16:36.708 --> 16:38.749
who question the canapé selection.

16:38.750 --> 16:41.791
There's this one lady who keeps
wanting to cap the gift registry.

16:43.750 --> 16:44.833
I'm gonna shut up now.

16:49.541 --> 16:51.166
She always wanted a girl.

16:56.625 --> 16:59.207
Show us the footage
from Rachel Mills's visit.

16:59.208 --> 17:02.750
Two visits, two video files.
Here's the first one.

17:04.583 --> 17:07.207
Huh, that's weird.
The video player won't open the file.

17:07.208 --> 17:08.416
I can see that. Why?

17:09.000 --> 17:11.583
No idea. It's never happened before.
Let me try the other one.

17:14.041 --> 17:14.875
What the--

17:16.083 --> 17:17.915
- Hey, you can't just grab--
- All right.

17:17.916 --> 17:22.207
If the file is corrupt,
we might be able to repair it with a VLC.

17:22.208 --> 17:25.499
We just need to rename it as an AVI file,

17:25.500 --> 17:28.791
set preferences, and reopen.

17:31.541 --> 17:33.832
Shit. The files aren't corrupt.

17:33.833 --> 17:36.625
They were erased
a few hours before we got here.

17:38.125 --> 17:41.624
Don't look at me. I took one online class
to learn the system. One.

17:41.625 --> 17:44.207
- Who's had access to the files?
- Any officer can access them.

17:44.208 --> 17:45.416
That narrows it down.

17:46.208 --> 17:47.708
Who escorted Burroughs down here?

17:48.875 --> 17:50.125
Officer Wesson.

17:50.833 --> 17:53.499
The same Ted Wesson
that Burroughs attacked last night?

17:53.500 --> 17:54.416
Yeah.

17:54.916 --> 17:57.415
- Where's Officer Wesson now?
- He went home this morning.

17:57.416 --> 18:00.333
Go to Officer Wesson's house
and drag his ass back here.

18:12.875 --> 18:14.375
There's no car out front.

18:16.541 --> 18:17.750
Maybe he's not home.

18:19.166 --> 18:21.207
Do you know if he has a family?

18:21.208 --> 18:23.083
He's married. He has a daughter.

18:24.666 --> 18:25.999
He told you he has a kid?

18:26.000 --> 18:29.833
I mean, in the context of it, he never
beat her to death with a baseball bat.

18:30.583 --> 18:31.541
Jesus.

18:32.458 --> 18:34.040
David, if his daughter's inside--

18:34.041 --> 18:36.500
He worked for the people who took Matthew.
He made his bed.

18:38.208 --> 18:39.541
Hey.

18:40.750 --> 18:42.291
I didn't sign up for that.

18:45.000 --> 18:46.666
Do we understand each other?

19:12.291 --> 19:14.374
Keep straight. You're almost there.

19:14.375 --> 19:15.458
Yes, ma'am.

19:16.625 --> 19:19.790
Simmons, you call me ma'am one more time,
I'm gonna toss your ass out this car.

19:19.791 --> 19:20.833
You understand?

20:00.458 --> 20:01.957
- Don't move, asshole!
- Okay.

20:01.958 --> 20:04.915
- You put the gun down. Do it now!
- Okay, yeah, okay. Easy.

20:04.916 --> 20:05.999
Slowly.

20:06.000 --> 20:08.457
Easy, easy. Okay?

20:08.458 --> 20:09.750
Turn around.

20:10.833 --> 20:12.083
Burroughs.

20:12.833 --> 20:14.208
What the hell are you doing here?

20:14.791 --> 20:18.082
The people who ordered you to kill me.

20:18.083 --> 20:20.207
- Do you know who they are?
- I have no idea.

20:20.208 --> 20:22.832
And I wish I had killed you because
if I had, I wouldn't be in this mess.

20:22.833 --> 20:24.082
You know where my son is?

20:24.083 --> 20:27.415
All I know is they've been watching you
since the day you arrived.

20:27.416 --> 20:29.957
And I was just supposed
to keep an eye on you. I was…

20:29.958 --> 20:32.415
I was supposed to babysit a child killer.

20:32.416 --> 20:36.040
And then your goddamn sister-in-law
shows up with that goddamn photograph.

20:36.041 --> 20:38.124
- And they want you dead.
- Is my son alive?

20:38.125 --> 20:40.999
I don't know. I am just doing
what they're telling me to do.

20:41.000 --> 20:42.291
How do you contact them?

20:49.333 --> 20:50.540
- Call them.
- I can't do that.

20:50.541 --> 20:52.999
- Yeah, you can.
- I can't. I need to protect my family!

20:53.000 --> 20:54.999
Look, you don't have to do this.
Please, listen.

20:55.000 --> 20:56.415
It's too late.

20:56.416 --> 20:59.124
- You can help me find my son.
- It's too late.

20:59.125 --> 21:01.999
I'm a loose end, and you have no idea
the reach these people have.

21:02.000 --> 21:04.250
- You never should've come here, Burroughs.
- What?

21:26.666 --> 21:28.125
David.

21:31.125 --> 21:32.333
He shot himself.

21:34.625 --> 21:36.083
Make a left, right here.

21:36.708 --> 21:38.125
7025.

21:44.500 --> 21:45.915
David, we have to go.

21:45.916 --> 21:48.250
Come on. Let's go. Come on.

21:53.416 --> 21:55.083
Ted Wesson!

22:11.125 --> 22:12.750
He's gone. Call it in.

22:26.291 --> 22:27.750
Damn it!

22:29.541 --> 22:31.707
- Why did he do that?
- They threatened his family.

22:31.708 --> 22:32.708
So he shot himself?

22:33.500 --> 22:34.790
To protect them.

22:34.791 --> 22:36.375
Did he tell you who has Matthew?

22:40.500 --> 22:41.500
No.

22:43.416 --> 22:44.791
They're covering their tracks.

22:46.416 --> 22:48.916
We gotta find Hilde Winslow
before they do.

23:04.583 --> 23:06.582
I want everything boxed and inventoried.

23:06.583 --> 23:07.583
Yes, sir.

23:09.583 --> 23:12.707
What time did Wesson take Burroughs
to the infirmary last night?

23:12.708 --> 23:14.000
Not sure.

23:15.500 --> 23:17.040
He forgot to sign him out.

23:17.041 --> 23:18.208
Forgot?

23:18.791 --> 23:19.832
It happens.

23:19.833 --> 23:21.000
Right.

23:32.791 --> 23:34.207
Psst. Hey.

23:34.208 --> 23:35.874
Did you happen to see Officer Wesson

23:35.875 --> 23:38.332
take David Burroughs
to the infirmary last night?

23:38.333 --> 23:39.750
I might have.

23:40.458 --> 23:42.041
I got trouble remembering things.

23:43.166 --> 23:45.666
Anything I can do to help jog your memory?

23:46.666 --> 23:50.208
Burroughs… has a flashlight.

23:51.791 --> 23:53.500
For reading after lights out.

23:54.208 --> 23:55.624
Can you get it for me?

23:55.625 --> 23:58.041
Come on, man, you know how this works.
Depends on what you saw.

24:01.250 --> 24:03.457
Wesson came for him
in the middle of the night.

24:03.458 --> 24:06.124
Which is strange, but not unheard of.

24:06.125 --> 24:08.291
But then he opens up his cell
with his emergency key.

24:10.208 --> 24:13.665
Instead of having the shift guard
buzz him in from the panel.

24:13.666 --> 24:17.082
Exactly. Now why would he do that
unless things wasn't on the up and up?

24:17.083 --> 24:19.000
You know what I'm saying?

24:19.708 --> 24:21.499
Let me get you that flashlight.

24:21.500 --> 24:23.790
Hey, you on your way
back here with Wesson?

24:23.791 --> 24:24.707
No.

24:24.708 --> 24:27.374
- What do you mean no? Why not?
- Because he's dead.

24:27.375 --> 24:29.000
He-- What?

24:29.541 --> 24:30.457
How?

24:30.458 --> 24:32.333
Single gunshot wound to the head.

24:34.875 --> 24:37.915
- Do we know who shot him?
- Have to wait for the ME and GSR.

24:37.916 --> 24:41.457
But a neighbor saw a man
matching David Burroughs's description

24:41.458 --> 24:43.582
enter the home minutes
before hearing a shot.

24:43.583 --> 24:45.499
You gotta be shitting me.

24:45.500 --> 24:47.540
And he wasn't alone.
Drove off with a woman.

24:47.541 --> 24:48.833
Rachel Mills.

24:50.291 --> 24:52.582
Any chance we can get them
before they hit the back roads?

24:52.583 --> 24:55.582
APB's out there, but our team
is spread across a 200-mile perimeter.

24:55.583 --> 24:57.665
No one thought he'd be
crazy enough to come back here.

24:57.666 --> 24:58.500
Yeah.

24:59.541 --> 25:01.832
Why would he risk coming back
just to kill Wesson?

25:01.833 --> 25:04.583
I'll dig into Wesson
and see what I can find.

25:08.958 --> 25:10.208
How long to New York?

25:10.875 --> 25:12.000
Couple hours.

25:13.458 --> 25:14.583
You okay?

25:19.583 --> 25:20.583
You sure?

25:23.541 --> 25:25.208
Yeah. It's just intense.

25:27.041 --> 25:28.125
What Wesson did.

25:31.166 --> 25:32.791
Hit a little close to home.

25:34.750 --> 25:35.833
Yeah, how so?

25:36.791 --> 25:39.415
Mackenzie didn't tell you
how I was fired from The Globe, did he?

25:39.416 --> 25:40.416
No.

25:43.333 --> 25:47.666
I was investigating a series
of sexual assaults at Lemhall University.

25:49.291 --> 25:51.540
The faculty and a bunch
of powerful boosters

25:51.541 --> 25:53.790
were trying to sweep it all under the rug.

25:53.791 --> 25:57.875
One of the victims was this junior
named Catherine Tullo,

25:58.625 --> 26:00.499
who didn't want to come forward.

26:00.500 --> 26:04.375
You know? She didn't want to face
the scrutiny of victim-blaming.

26:07.458 --> 26:09.000
But I-I pushed her.

26:11.833 --> 26:13.083
I really pushed.

26:17.000 --> 26:19.833
Until she agreed to go on the record.

26:20.958 --> 26:22.083
Um…

26:24.333 --> 26:26.791
And the night before
we were supposed to meet,

26:28.041 --> 26:29.333
Catherine took her own life.

26:33.125 --> 26:34.624
I pushed her too hard.

26:34.625 --> 26:35.666
It was…

26:40.166 --> 26:41.875
All I could see was the story.

26:42.541 --> 26:44.041
You can't blame yourself.

26:44.833 --> 26:46.083
Her parents did.

26:48.125 --> 26:52.000
They sued The Globe
for wrongful death, and I lost my job.

26:54.708 --> 26:56.208
They lost their daughter.

26:59.625 --> 27:02.791
You're a good person, Rachel.

27:07.250 --> 27:09.291
Even if you're
aiding and abetting a fugitive.

27:16.583 --> 27:17.875
Where'd that come from?

27:18.791 --> 27:19.833
It's Wesson's.

27:29.166 --> 27:30.999
Mr. Burroughs, I presume?

27:31.000 --> 27:34.125
- Who's this?
- I heard you paid Officer Wesson a visit.

27:36.041 --> 27:37.958
The police think you killed him.

27:38.625 --> 27:40.583
That should speed
your capture along nicely.

27:41.541 --> 27:44.166
- Where's Matthew?
- Oh, David.

27:44.750 --> 27:46.833
Your son died five years ago.

27:47.833 --> 27:49.333
You beat him to death, remember?

27:52.166 --> 27:53.666
I'm gonna find you.

27:55.541 --> 27:58.665
Even if you did, it wouldn't matter.

27:58.666 --> 28:01.332
The fact you think it would
shows how naive you are.

28:01.333 --> 28:04.708
How little you understand
what you are up against.

28:06.541 --> 28:08.291
I'm coming for my son.

28:10.541 --> 28:11.958
I'm coming for Matthew.

28:18.916 --> 28:21.207
Looks like
there won't be any opportunity for rain.

28:21.208 --> 28:24.915
The next time you're probably gonna
need your rain gear will be Friday.

28:24.916 --> 28:26.999
And in the city, we might have rain…

28:27.000 --> 28:29.250
Still nothing on the local news
about your escape.

28:29.875 --> 28:31.707
So where's Hilde's PO box?

28:31.708 --> 28:32.750
Midtown.

28:34.250 --> 28:36.208
Doesn't open until 9:00 a.m.

28:37.041 --> 28:38.375
So we need a place to crash.

28:39.666 --> 28:40.958
I guess we sleep in the car.

28:42.875 --> 28:44.583
Maybe not. Do you remember Hayden?

28:45.166 --> 28:46.249
Yeah.

28:46.250 --> 28:47.583
What are you thinking?

28:48.916 --> 28:51.958
I'm thinking we need a burner phone.

28:57.958 --> 28:58.791
You okay?

28:59.375 --> 29:01.750
Yeah, it's-- It's just a bit much.

29:02.333 --> 29:05.707
You know, I… kind of forgot
what real life looks like.

29:05.708 --> 29:08.790
To be fair, I just saw a woman's dog
wearing a Gucci sweater,

29:08.791 --> 29:10.875
so real life might be a stretch.

29:11.916 --> 29:13.083
Oh, there's a kiosk.

29:44.083 --> 29:47.041
Hey. Can I get a prepaid phone, please?

29:52.541 --> 29:56.582
And finally,
we have Hendrick Sorgh's A Kitchen.

29:56.583 --> 29:59.040
Shall we start the bidding at $500,000?

29:59.041 --> 30:02.000
$500,000. $550,000.

30:03.416 --> 30:04.833
$600,000.

30:05.708 --> 30:07.250
$650,000.

30:07.875 --> 30:09.166
$700,000.

30:10.208 --> 30:11.624
$800,000.

30:11.625 --> 30:13.000
1.5.

30:13.500 --> 30:15.958
$1.5 million.

30:16.708 --> 30:17.791
Going once.

30:18.750 --> 30:19.875
Twice.

30:20.375 --> 30:22.291
Sold.

30:25.666 --> 30:27.499
- Hayden.
- Rachel.

30:27.500 --> 30:29.082
It's good to hear from you.

30:29.083 --> 30:32.541
Hey. I should have called you
a long time ago, um…

30:33.375 --> 30:35.957
After The Globe,
I know I sort of disappeared.

30:35.958 --> 30:38.874
No, no, no. No apologies necessary.

30:38.875 --> 30:43.082
Hey, listen, I'm in Boston right now.
How about, uh, we get a drink, catch up?

30:43.083 --> 30:45.874
You know, I wish I could.
I'm actually in New York,

30:45.875 --> 30:48.000
which is the reason I'm calling.

30:48.583 --> 30:51.124
Why do I feel a favor coming on?

30:51.125 --> 30:52.457
Yeah, it's a crazy story.

30:52.458 --> 30:55.749
I had my purse stolen,
and without my ID and my credit card,

30:55.750 --> 30:57.082
I can't check into my hotel.

30:57.083 --> 30:59.582
So, I know this is a big ask,
but is there any way

30:59.583 --> 31:01.582
I could stay at your place
just for the night?

31:01.583 --> 31:02.708
Yeah, of course.

31:03.500 --> 31:06.249
Hey, look, I'll come down tomorrow
and we'll grab a bite.

31:06.250 --> 31:10.582
You know, I'd love that, but I'm just
here literally just for the night.

31:10.583 --> 31:12.374
Um, but maybe another time?

31:12.375 --> 31:13.708
I'm gonna hold you to it.

31:15.083 --> 31:16.083
Um…

31:16.666 --> 31:18.791
I'll have the spare keys left
at the front desk for you.

31:20.375 --> 31:22.957
- Thank you, Hayden.
- Yeah, anytime.

31:22.958 --> 31:24.458
And hey, Rachel, it's…

31:25.375 --> 31:27.916
- It's really good to hear from you.
- Yeah, you too.

31:29.333 --> 31:30.166
Bye.

31:30.708 --> 31:32.291
Hey, we're all set.

31:38.500 --> 31:39.416
Yeah.

31:40.166 --> 31:41.708
All right, thanks, Chopra.

31:42.625 --> 31:43.541
No sign of him.

31:45.333 --> 31:46.333
Thanks.

31:47.458 --> 31:52.165
So, I was doing some digging into Wesson,
and I found something odd.

31:52.166 --> 31:53.707
He's been getting $1,000 a month

31:53.708 --> 31:57.249
for the last five years
from this company called REH Holdings.

31:57.250 --> 31:58.915
Sounds like a shell company.

31:58.916 --> 32:01.083
Mm-hmm. It's registered in the Caymans.

32:01.708 --> 32:03.374
It's untraceable even for us.

32:03.375 --> 32:04.374
Hmm.

32:04.375 --> 32:07.250
The payments started the month
that Burroughs arrived at Briggs.

32:08.291 --> 32:10.208
You think someone's paying
to keep tabs on him?

32:11.083 --> 32:13.041
I'm saying the timing lines up.

32:14.708 --> 32:16.790
You know, you might be right about that.

32:16.791 --> 32:17.999
Don't hear that often.

32:18.000 --> 32:20.499
I talked to the inmate
next to Burroughs's cell.

32:20.500 --> 32:21.874
Mm-hmm.

32:21.875 --> 32:26.500
He told me Wesson came and got him out
of his cell in the middle of the night.

32:27.208 --> 32:30.207
But he used his emergency key
to open the cell door

32:30.208 --> 32:31.958
instead of getting it buzzed open.

32:33.166 --> 32:34.583
He wanted it off the books.

32:37.541 --> 32:41.708
What if Wesson tried to kill Burroughs
last night and not the other way around?

32:42.416 --> 32:47.040
Maybe Burroughs decides to hang around
and settle the score.

32:47.041 --> 32:49.208
Yeah, definitely possible.

32:51.083 --> 32:53.665
But it doesn't say anything
about where he's going next.

32:53.666 --> 32:57.415
I don't suppose this inmate of yours
told you where he was headed?

32:57.416 --> 32:58.541
No.

32:59.958 --> 33:04.374
Goddamn it. I promised the guy
I'd get him Burroughs's flashlight.

33:04.375 --> 33:05.208
Well…

33:10.625 --> 33:11.665
What?

33:11.666 --> 33:16.083
Briggs sent over the inventory list
from Burroughs's cell a couple hours ago.

33:19.541 --> 33:22.041
There's no flashlight on this list.

33:23.208 --> 33:25.166
We toss the cell every week.

33:25.750 --> 33:28.541
If he's hiding something,
it's a surprise to me.

33:29.500 --> 33:31.625
Let's start with the mattress.

33:59.875 --> 34:01.083
Here we go.

34:04.708 --> 34:05.583
Huh.

34:09.333 --> 34:10.583
What is it?

34:11.375 --> 34:13.291
It's his son's case file.

34:15.125 --> 34:17.582
Hey. He circled this name.

34:17.583 --> 34:19.124
Hilde Winslow.

34:19.125 --> 34:21.499
That's the witness
who saw him bury the bat.

34:21.500 --> 34:23.332
Her testimony helped put him away.

34:23.333 --> 34:25.750
If he killed Wesson to settle the score,
she might be next.

34:50.041 --> 34:52.250
Yeah, it's a lot, right?

34:59.541 --> 35:00.958
Empty fridge.

35:03.250 --> 35:04.916
As usual, nothing.

35:08.166 --> 35:11.833
I'm gonna pop out to the bodega and see
if I can scrounge something up for dinner.

35:16.375 --> 35:17.208
You good?

35:20.333 --> 35:21.583
Matthew's out there.

35:23.750 --> 35:24.875
Somewhere.

35:29.791 --> 35:31.291
Be right back.

35:45.416 --> 35:47.290
Nothing on David getting caught.

35:47.291 --> 35:49.582
Should've never
gotten you involved in any of this.

35:49.583 --> 35:51.249
A little late for that, old man.

35:51.250 --> 35:52.582
I'm serious, Adam.
They could take your shield.

35:52.583 --> 35:53.957
At the very least,
they're gonna suspend you.

35:53.958 --> 35:55.040
I know.

35:55.041 --> 35:56.000
Adam.

35:57.041 --> 35:59.250
It's David. He's family.

36:01.375 --> 36:03.332
Did he tell you
who he thought was behind this?

36:03.333 --> 36:04.208
No.

36:22.166 --> 36:23.707
You gonna be okay in my guest room?

36:23.708 --> 36:25.582
Where are you going?

36:25.583 --> 36:27.499
Uh, I got something to take care of.

36:27.500 --> 36:28.666
At this hour?

36:30.958 --> 36:32.125
I'll see you later, Pops.

36:44.875 --> 36:46.500
Hey, I'm back.

37:19.375 --> 37:20.583
I borrowed some clothes.

37:21.166 --> 37:23.000
- I hope that's okay.
- Of course.

37:28.541 --> 37:30.040
And we have breaking news.

37:30.041 --> 37:32.124
Convicted child killer David Burroughs

37:32.125 --> 37:35.290
escaped Briggs Penitentiary
earlier this morning.

37:35.291 --> 37:37.707
Police are still
on the hunt for Burroughs,

37:37.708 --> 37:39.999
whose whereabouts remain unknown.

37:40.000 --> 37:42.249
In a news conference this evening…

37:42.250 --> 37:43.457
Don't look at that.

37:43.458 --> 37:45.333
…their search has widened…

37:45.916 --> 37:48.083
Bodega dinner. All right.

37:50.250 --> 37:51.916
Looks great.

37:52.625 --> 37:54.499
You know what? Hayden's gotta have
a bottle of something

37:54.500 --> 37:56.166
that's gonna make this
taste very expensive.

37:56.875 --> 37:59.499
Officials have warned that anyone found

37:59.500 --> 38:02.415
to be aiding or abetting Burroughs
in his escape

38:02.416 --> 38:04.375
will be arrested and prosecuted to the…

38:05.458 --> 38:07.707
Chopin martini. Dry, three olives, please.

38:07.708 --> 38:09.291
- Thanks.
- Coming up.

38:10.208 --> 38:13.707
…murderer escaped
from Briggs Penitentiary earlier today

38:13.708 --> 38:15.624
and is still considered a danger…

38:15.625 --> 38:18.540
The FBI has not yet
made an official statement,

38:18.541 --> 38:20.249
but the search remains ongoing.

38:20.250 --> 38:22.165
Those with information on Burroughs

38:22.166 --> 38:25.665
are encouraged to contact
their local police department.

38:25.666 --> 38:29.291
Authorities are calling this
an all-hands-on-deck situation…

38:45.041 --> 38:45.916
Hey.

38:47.250 --> 38:48.333
We're gonna find him.

38:49.833 --> 38:50.916
Together.

39:14.708 --> 39:16.457
I watched you…

39:16.458 --> 39:19.458
Philip, what the hell's going on?

39:20.166 --> 39:21.583
Call me back.

39:22.416 --> 39:27.000
Into a fly

39:29.208 --> 39:32.458
I looked away

39:34.041 --> 39:38.000
You were on fire

39:52.208 --> 39:53.125
Yeah.

39:54.875 --> 39:56.125
I'm almost done here.

39:58.208 --> 40:00.041
Yes, I understand.

40:02.166 --> 40:04.000
It's being taken care of.

40:10.375 --> 40:14.166
I took you home

40:16.625 --> 40:19.916
Then I laughed

40:21.458 --> 40:25.790
I watched a change

40:25.791 --> 40:28.166
In you

40:29.041 --> 40:32.582
It's like you never

40:32.583 --> 40:35.499
Had wings

40:35.500 --> 40:42.415
Ah, ah, ah

40:42.416 --> 40:44.333
Ah, ah
